lane: channel-ring-unbounded
why: the one lane still behind zio.Queue is StmChannel at chunk
  granularity (130.6 vs 122.2), and after channel-sentinel-default
  that mechanism is reached only by UNBOUNDED channels -- which is
  what Channel.apply defaults to. Its cost is List.reverse, 40% of
  leaf samples, and it cannot be fixed inside the model: the reverse
  is amortized one per element and three earlier lanes failed trying
  to swap the structure. So the unbounded case needs a ring too.
how: Segments -- a linked list of fixed arrays behind the same
  position counters, so a claim is still one atomic and popMany still
  takes a run with one CAS. Segments are NEVER reused or freed by
  hand: a scanner holds its segment by reference and the GC reclaims
  what nobody holds, which is what keeps the use-after-free class out
  of this entirely. A Buffer seam lets SentinelChannel take either.
  Must pass both law tiers, bounded and unbounded, before the default
  moves.
